{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 40, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Verily then dost thou crave a journey’s tale most fair\nThrough lands where cherry blossoms kiss the air\nHark now and heed this plan most tight and sweet\nAs thy voyage through Nippon’s realms dost beat.\n\n**Upon the morrow first dost thou arise**\nTo Tokyo fair where neon lights do blaze\nUnto Shibuya’s heart thou shalt repair\nWhere scramble crossings weave their magic rare.\nBehold the towers tall where dreams take flight\nAnd quaff some sake ‘neath lanterns bright.\n\n**The second morn thy steeds thou dost prepare**\nTo Asakusa’s streets both old and dear\nWhere Sensō-ji’s gates do stand so grand\nAnd temple bells their hymns unto the land.\nPeruse the stores where craftsmen’s hands do toil\nAnd sample delicacies most subtle and royal.\n\n**On the third day forth thou shalt depart**\nTo Nikko’s woods where kami’s whispers art\nThe shrines of Toshogu with gold aglow\nAnd bridges cross the waters soft and slow.\nWalk where time doth linger still and deep\nAmong the cedars that the ancients keep.\n\n**Behold the fourth where Kyoto’s splendor plays**\nThe Golden Pavilion gleams in dawn’s array\nUnto Fushimi’s slopes where sacred streams do flow\nAnd priests perform their rites both soft and slow.\nThrough Gion’s lanes where geishas tread so light\nAnd tea is served with honeyed pure delight.\n\n**The fifth day calls thee to Nara’s embrace**\nWhere deer in parks do freely roam with grace\nUnto Todai-ji’s hall so vast and wide\nWhere Buddha’s gaze doth guard the sacred tide.\nFeed the creatures gentle as thyself thou art\nAnd lose thyself in nature’s vast work art.\n\n**On to Osaka thine journey next doth bear**\nWhere castle stands o’er portals wide and fair\nSample takoyaki’s ball where flavors blend\nAnd dotonbori’s lights where dreams depend.\nThe Universal Studios call thy name\nWhere heroes walk and laughter’s sweet as fame.\n\n**The sixth day sees thee to Hiroshima’s shore**\nWhere peace and memory forevermore do dwell\nThe museum’s halls where shadows tell their tale\nAnd cranes of paper soar where love doth sail.\nThe Miyajima’s torii red in waters gleam\nA fleeting touch of heaven’s holy dream.\n\n**Return once more to Kyoto fair and bright**\nWhere Arashiyama’s forests wrap thee in their might\nThe bamboo groves where whispers drift on air\nAnd temples stand where monks do meditate with care.\nThy final eve be spent in Pontochō’s glow\nWhere lanterns cast their soft and dreamy show.\n\n**Thus ends thy journey through this land divine**\nWhere ancient meets the future ever so fine.\nWith memories rich and heart both full and free\nThou’lt bear this tale back home to where thou’st be.\nFarewell now traveler for thy path is set\nIn Nippon’s grace thou’lt find thyself well met.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ver", "logprob": -3.722797155380249}, {"token": "ily", "logprob": -0.00019238528329879045}, {"token": " then", "logprob": -2.7191548347473145}, {"token": " dost", "logprob": -3.3884530067443848}, {"token": " thou", "logprob": -0.027439581230282784}, {"token": " cra", "logprob": -2.1550729274749756}, {"token": "ve", "logprob": -0.0004107108688913286}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.4333666265010834}, {"token": " journey", "logprob": -1.4233756065368652}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -2.9511187076568604}, {"token": " tale", "logprob": -1.2668254375457764}, {"token": " most", "logprob": -0.7504664063453674}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -0.42907655239105225}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.12146125733852386}, {"token": "Through", "logprob": -1.3944010734558105}, {"token": " lands", "logprob": -0.8006627559661865}, {"token": " where", "logprob": -0.07915157824754715}, {"token": " cherry", "logprob": -0.05736143887042999}, {"token": " bloss", "logprob": -0.1829828917980194}, {"token": "oms", "logprob": -0.002012729411944747}, {"token": " kiss", "logprob": -1.4671235084533691}, {"token": " the", "logprob